Title: THE GLASS KEY
Author: Helen Voss
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. ASHWORTH MANOR - ESTABLISHING - DAY

Gothic stone. Rain. A single police cruiser in the drive.

INT. MANOR - LIBRARY - DAY

Empty velvet case. MRS. ASHWORTH watches DETECTIVE MAYA QUINN work.
MAYA
The GLASS KEY was here at midnight. Who had access?

INT. MANOR - DINING ROOM - DAY

Quinn interviews the nephew, CALEB, 40s, nervous cuff adjustment.
CALEB
I left after port. I didn't need heirloom drama.

INT. MANOR - GREENHOUSE - DAY

TOMAS, 22, the gardener. Mud, locket, defensive posture.
TOMAS
I lock up at nine.

INT. MANOR - SERVANTS' STAIR - DAY

Quinn finds a muddy partial print — smaller than Tomas's boot.
MAYA
Someone ran through here after the rain started.

INT. MANOR - NORTH WING HALL - DAY

Scratches on the portrait frame. Hidden door behind MR. ASHWORTH's likeness.

INT. HIDDEN STUDY - DAY

Decoy GLASS KEY. Cryptic note on the desk.
MAYA
This room hasn't been opened in years. Except tonight.

INT. MANOR - MRS. ASHWORTH'S BEDROOM - DAY

Quinn finds a ledger entry — insurance revised upward last week.
MAYA
You reported the key missing before you called us.

INT. MANOR - LIBRARY - DAY

Caleb bursts in — heard about the hidden study.
CALEB
That key opens a safe with my inheritance. I'm the only son.

INT. MANOR - LIBRARY - DAY

Maya lays decoy and empty case before Mrs. Ashworth. The old woman's composure cracks — not grief, but calculation.
MAYA
The print on the stair matched Tomas exactly. And a nineteen-year-old gardener didn't revise your insurance. You moved the key to delay the reading. The question is who you're protecting.

FADE OUT.


THE END
